~ start
set locals.proceedable = 0
set locals.fee = 5
if not TagManager.has_tag(GameTags.Dialogue.NPC_DRONEWORKS_MET):
	Manager: A million credits.
	=> meeting
else:
	Manager: Hi
	=> more

~ more
- So, what are your services?
	set locals.proceedable = 1
	Manager: We build ships. Drones. Autonomous defense and offensive crafts.
	Manager: Our current catalogue includes 3 out of the 50 models that are currently in circulation.
	=> more
- How do I know I didn't just fund a terrorist?
	Manager: Funny.
	You: No, seriously. Are you a terrorist?
	Manager: Sure.
	You: I want my money back.
	Manager: You should not negotiate with terrorists.
	=> more
- What... are you?
	Manager: No, what are you?
	You: I captain the generational ship requisitioned to me for the express purpose of defending against the invasion fleet. If necessary, my ship and I will be the last barrier between the invaders and our sun. You... don't know about the generational ship program?
	Manager: Nah, I'm just messing with you. Glad to be of service, captain. I just had to make sure you were the real deal. No other entity in the galaxy would [wave amp=25 freq=5]willingly[/wave] donate {{locals.fee}} scrap, after all.
	You: [The simple reveal that you are not dealing with an idiot fills you with relief and renewed determination]
	=> more
- When [if locals.proceedable == 1] will you be updating your catalogue?
	set locals.proceedable = 2
	Manager: Whenever I get more investment.
	=> more
- Can [if locals.proceedable == 2 or locals.proceedable == 3]I invest any more?
	set locals.fee = 1000
	set locals.proceedable += 1
	Manager: Sure, it'll be {{locals.fee}} scraps.
	You: That's a steep increase.
	Manager: You asked for it. 
	=> more
- So [if locals.proceedable == 2 or locals.proceedable == 3]if I buy all of your drones, and you find all the investment you need, what happens then?
	set locals.proceedable += 1
	Manager: The drones ain't cheap, captain, and I feel you're approaching this from a point of extreme privilege.
	You: It's not like I have caviar for breakfast. [wait=0.5]It's for dinner only.
	=> more

- Seriously, [if locals.proceedable >= 4]I want more ships in my fleet. What can I do?
	Manager: 1000 scraps. I've already told you that. 
	Manager: That's how much seed money I got from my first investor.
	Manager: [He looks into the distance, as if remembering a bad memory]
	Manager: Except it wasn't really seed money.
	You: What do you mean?
	Manager: A year ago, I found this unmarked credit transport on its way to an inner system shipyard. It had hit a debris field and the engines were offline.
	Manager: I hauled the wreck to a cutter and came out 1000 scraps richer. It was unmarked, perfectly legal to salvage.
	Manager: It turns out that I wasn't the only one who had eyes on that ship. I tripped a whole lot of alarms, they were onto me before long.
	You: And now they're very angry with you.
	Manager: Oh no. They were very impressed, actually. I just have to pay them back tenfold, or they'll blow the station. They rigged it with a few kilotons for insurance, you see.
	You: They're holding you hostage with nukes? STAY VERY STILL. I'll call in support from the fleet.
	Manager: No, no, it's just regular plastic explosives, and it's quite far away from the living quarters. Calm down.
	Manager: Anyways, you've asked, and now you know. Please don't go spill my secrets elsewhere. I trust you because you're [b]the[/b] captain.
	- I'll get you 1000 scraps
		Manager: And I'll upgrade you to a [color="gold"]pro plus max user.[/color]
	- I'll bring them to justice. Who am I looking for?
		Manager: Good luck. But I'm not snitching. In my eyes, I've fucked around and found out.
	- I'm sorry. I can't do anything.
		Manager: It's fine. I didn't ask for any help in the first place. Go buy another drone or something.
	Manager: I have to say though, it'll be a while before I upgrade my catalogue. Investment or not, these things take time.
	
~ meeting
You: Huh?
Manager: A million credits. That's my price.
set locals.fee = 5
You: I only have scraps.
Manager: ...Fine. That'll be {{locals.fee}} scraps.
=> questions

~ questions
- That's surprisingly low.
	set locals.fee += 5
	Manager: Fine. It's {{locals.fee}} scraps now.
	=> questions
- What's that for?
	Manager: An investment.
	=> questions
- Sure [pay {{locals.fee}} scrap]
	if ResourceManager.spend("scrap", locals.fee)
		do TagManager.add_tag(GameTags.Dialogue.NPC_DRONEWORKS_MET)
		Manager: Well appreciated.
		=> proceed
	else
		Manager: What are you, broke? Fine. I'll do a discount.
		set locals.fee -= 1
		=> questions
		
~ proceed
You: So what did I just buy?
Manager: Technically, you bought nothing.
You: What?
Manager: Think of it as a pay-as-you-go subscription to access my services.
=> more